      "text": "## CRM pricing comparison for consultants\n\n**Prices checked September 5, 2026.** Amounts are USD per user/month unless noted; annual prices generally require upfront annual payment.\n\n| CRM | Free option | Paid pricing | Consultant-oriented take |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| **Bigin by Zoho** | Free for 1 user | **$7\u2013$18 billed annually**; monthly plans run **$9\u2013$21**. ([bigin.com](https://www.bigin.com/articles/faqs-about-bigin.html?utm_source=openai)) | Lowest-cost choice for a solo consultant needing contacts, pipelines and basic automation. |\n| **HubSpot Sales Hub** | Free for up to 2 users | Currently displayed at **$7\u2013$150**; Professional and Enterprise also require **$1,500\u2013$3,500** one-time onboarding. ([hubspot.com](https://www.hubspot.com/pricing/sales?iframe=yes)) | Attractive free CRM, but advanced automation becomes expensive quickly. |\n| **Freshsales** | Free for up to 3 users | **$9\u2013$59 billed annually**. ([freshworks.com](https://www.freshworks.com/crm/pricing-compare/)) | Good value for a small consultancy wanting email, phone, chat and pipeline features together. |\n| **monday CRM** | 14-day trial | **$12\u2013$28 billed annually** or **$18\u2013$41 billed monthly**; plans start at 3 users. ([monday.com](https://monday.com/crm/pricing)) | Flexible for firms combining business development with project-style workflows, but the 3-seat minimum hurts solo consultants. |\n| **Pipedrive** | 14-day trial | **$14\u2013$79 billed annually**. ([pipedrive.com](https://www.pipedrive.com/en/pricing?utm_source=openai)) | Strong pipeline-focused option for consultants with a structured lead, proposal and follow-up process. |\n| **Zoho CRM** | Free for up to 3 users | **$14\u2013$52** across Standard through Ultimate editions. ([zoho.com](https://www.zoho.com/crm/zohocrm-pricing-calculator.html?utm_source=openai)) | Broad functionality at moderate prices; useful when you expect to add automation, quoting or customer portals. |\n| **Less Annoying CRM** | 30-day trial | Flat **$15**, billed monthly with no long-term contract. ([lessannoyingcrm.com](https://lessannoyingcrm.com/help/pricing)) | Most predictable pricing and one of the simplest choices for independent consultants. |\n| **Copper** | Trial only | **$23\u2013$99 billed annually** or **$29\u2013$134 billed monthly**. ([copper.com](https://www.copper.com/pricing?ref_lead_source=fb)) | Pricier, but its plans combine pipelines with task automation and project-management capabilities. |\n| **Salesforce** | Free Suite available | **$25\u2013$550**; Starter is $25, Pro is $100 and Enterprise is $175. ([salesforce.com](https://www.salesforce.com/sales/pricing/?bc=OTH&d=cta-body-promo-8)) | Usually excessive for an independent consultant, but relevant for larger consultancies needing extensive customization and integrations. |\n\n### Quick recommendations\n\n- **Best for one consultant:** Bigin at **$7\u2013$18** annually, or Less Annoying CRM at a predictable **$15** monthly.\n- **Best free starting point:** HubSpot for up to two users or Freshsales for up to three users.\n- **Best for sales-pipeline discipline:** Pipedrive at **$14\u2013$79** annually.\n- **Best balance of price and expandability:** Zoho CRM at **$14\u2013$52**.\n- **Best for CRM plus flexible workflows:** monday CRM, provided its three-user minimum is acceptable.\n- **Best for a growing consulting organization:** Salesforce or HubSpot Professional\u2014but onboarding and higher-tier costs require closer scrutiny."
